{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$g$ is a rational function.\n\nTo find the derivative of rational functions, we use **the quotient rule**:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)}\\right]\u0026=\\dfrac{\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)]v(x)-u(x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}[v(x)]}{[v(x)]^2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{u'(x)v(x)-u(x)v'(x)}{[v(x)]^2}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's differentiate!\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}g'(x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\dfrac{x-5}{x^2+1}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{(x^2+1)\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x-5)-(x-5)\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^2+1)}{(x^2+1)^2}\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{The quotient rule}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{(x^2+1)(1)-(x-5)(2x)}{(x^2+1)^2}\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Differentiate }(x-5)\\text{ \u0026 }(x^2+1)}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{x^2+1-2x^2+10x}{(x^2+1)^2}\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Expand}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1+10x-x^2}{(x^2+1)^2}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, $g'(x)=\\dfrac{1+10x-x^2}{(x^2+1)^2}$, or any other equivalent form.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $g(x)=\\dfrac{x-5}{x^2+1}$.\n\n$g'(x)=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"\\frac{1+10x-x^2}{\\left(x^2+1\\right)^2}"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
